// docs/architecture/csharp-migration/ownership-flip-runbook.md.
//
// Re-adding a model here is a `cross-owner collision` in `scripts/table-ownership.mjs` (red build),
// and it re-arms the §2 DROP TABLE hazard from the other direction.
//
// The repo's executable definition of the three tables now lives at
// services/Tims.Platform/db/flip-ddl/calibration.sql (runbook §0 P8) — apply it after
// `prisma db push` when bootstrapping a dev database.
//
// TENANCY, because it is non-standard and a "fix" would be a security regression:
// `calibration_members` and `calibration_votes` have NO `organization_id` column. Their RLS is a
// session-subquery policy (`EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM calibration_sessions par WHERE par.id = session_id
// AND par.organization_id = <GUC>)`) on BOTH `USING` and `WITH CHECK`. That `WITH CHECK` on the
// session linkage IS the tenant guard, and the C# write entities deliberately carry no
// `OrganizationId`. Do not normalise these tables.
//
// `NineBoxEvaluation` above is NOT part of this flip — `nine_box_evaluations` stays Prisma-owned.
